<figure><img src="https://baty.net/img/2026/20260725-fence.webp" alt="Black and white photo of a fence"><figcaption>Fence (2015). M3 testing Tri-X at 1600</figcaption></figure><p>Suddenly this morning, my Org Agenda was empty. It should never be empty. Emacs had already been running, idle, so I've no idea how it happened. A restart fixed it, but it was unsettling enough that I created a separate <code>blog</code> script to replace the emacs-dependent parts of my blogging workflow. Now I can do <code>blog journal</code> or <code>blog post</code> or <code>blog cover</code> in a terminal, and it does the right thing, then opens the file in <code>$VISUAL</code>. Feels safer this way. The Emacs functions were 90% just calling out to existing shell scripts anyway, so there's only a small amount of duplication.</p>
<hr />
<p>I've spent several hours this morning making stuff work on my Mac that already worked fine on Linux, because &quot;what if?&quot;. It's exhausting. On the plus side, I'm editing this post in BBEdit, which is always just so damn comfortable.</p>
